--From 5144127405262dc0adadea40c695d01a1181700d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
--From: Vincenzo Ceccarelli Grimaldi <vince.ceccarelli@gmail.com>
--Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 17:11:59 +0000
--Subject: [PATCH] fix(copy): six calculators, not seven
--
--Live verification of the deployed site caught the site miscounting its own
--tools. The Tools section holds six calculators; the homepage, About and
--Pricing pages each claimed seven, in both languages. The seventh was the
--grid-droop instrument, which lives under Resources as a lab instrument and
--was never a calculator.
--
--Corrected in all six places. On a site whose argument is that every number
--is either computed or cited, a headline that miscounts its own inventory
--is the most expensive kind of error to leave standing.
